<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE HermitCrabInput SYSTEM "HermitCrabInput.dtd">
<!-- Final-template partial discriminators. Pins HermitCrab's two final-template gates in
     SynthesisAffixProcessRule.cs: NonPartialRuleProhibitedAfterFinalTemplate and
     NonPartialRuleRequiredAfterNonFinalTemplate. Both gates fire only for a rule that is
     "ordinary" (AffixProcessRuleDef.is_template_rule == false, i.e. no AffixTemplate Slot anywhere
     references it), and only when that rule is tried immediately after a template has just applied
     to the same word. That ordering (a stratum-listed rule tried right after ApplyTemplates) is only
     reachable via the Unordered ApplyTemplates -> ApplyMorphologicalRules recursion in
     SynthesisStratumRule.cs (see morphotactic-attribute-breadth's own header comment for the same
     finding), so Main below is Unordered, not Linear.

     Three independent branches, isolated by PartsOfSpeech so a mutation to one branch's construct
     can never change another branch's words:

     Branch A (posX, root dak) pins NonPartialRuleProhibitedAfterFinalTemplate:
       - finalTemplateA (final="true") tags "fa"; mrGate1 (ordinary, non-partial) tags "ga".
       - dakfaga: mrGate1 tried right after finalTemplateA. Blocked (gate fires): a non-partial
         ordinary rule is prohibited after a final template.
       - daknagafa: the SAME mrGate1 tried right after nonFinalTemplateA (final="false") instead.
         Permitted, because the gate only fires when the template that just applied was final.
         finalTemplateA then completes the derivation (a template must still close it; see
         morphotactic-attribute-breadth's finding that a non-final-only stratum admits no complete
         word at all).

     Branch B (posY, root pil) pins NonPartialRuleRequiredAfterNonFinalTemplate, and also carries
     the fixture's first POSITIVE, partial-dependent word (pilfbvb, a parse that exists only
     because a rule is partial, needed to let FST recall be measured against a backend that could
     silently under-propose on partial-bearing grammars):
       - finalTemplateB (final="true") tags "fb"; nonFinalTemplateB (final="false") tags "nb".
       - mrGate2Partial (ordinary, partial="true") tags "vb"; mrGate2Complete (ordinary, NOT
         partial) tags "tb".
       - pilnbvbfb: mrGate2Partial tried right after nonFinalTemplateB. Blocked (gate fires): a
         partial ordinary rule cannot complete a non-final-template derivation.
       - pilnbtbfb: mrGate2Complete (non-partial) tried in the identical position. Permitted,
         because the gate only fires when the rule ITSELF is partial.
       - pilfbvb: mrGate2Partial tried right after finalTemplateB instead (the mirror of dakfaga,
         but with a partial rule). NonPartialRuleProhibitedAfterFinalTemplate does not fire because
         mrGate2Partial is partial, so unlike dakfaga this one parses.

     Branch C (posZ, root nib) pins the OTHER arm of SynthesisAffixTemplatesRule.cs's line-59
     pass-through: a partial WORD survives an applicable template battery that applies nothing,
     where a non-partial word would die with ApplicableTemplatesNotApplied instead. mrGate3Partial
     (ordinary, partial="true") tags "gi", making the word partial; templateZ is applicable to posZ
     (so applicableTemplate=true) but its one mandatory slot's rule (mrZTagSlot) can never match
     the word it is tried against, so the battery yields zero output regardless. nibgi is the
     second POSITIVE, partial-dependent word: it parses only because the word is partial when the
     empty battery is reached, per line 59's `!input.IsPartial && applicableTemplate` test.

     Every tag/slot rule (mrFinTagA/mrNonFinTagA/mrFinTagB/mrNonFinTagB/mrZTagSlot) is listed ONLY
     inside its own AffixTemplate Slot, never on the Stratum's own morphologicalRules attribute, so
     it stays IsTemplateRule=true and is exempt from both gates by construction (see
     template-category-sharing's own Stratum comment for the mechanism: a rule reachable ONLY
     through its own template's Slot must be omitted from the Stratum's morphologicalRules
     attribute, or it stays freely combinable and is no longer exclusive to that template). mrGate1/
     mrGate2Partial/mrGate2Complete/mrGate3Partial are the reverse: listed on the Stratum's
     morphologicalRules attribute and never a Slot member, so they are "ordinary" and squarely
     inside both gates' scope. (mrGate3Partial is never actually refused by either gate here: it is
     always the first rule tried, with no template applied before it. But it stays stratum-listed
     rather than template-only so its own IsPartial flag, not IsTemplateRule, is what the line-59
     pass-through cares about.) -->
<HermitCrabInput>
  <Language>
    <Name>FinalTemplatePartialDiscriminators</Name>
    <PartsOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posX"><Name>x</Name></PartOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posY"><Name>y</Name></PartOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posZ"><Name>z</Name></PartOfSpeech>
    </PartsOfSpeech>
    <CharacterDefinitionTable id="tbl">
      <Name>Main</Name>
      <SegmentDefinitions>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sA"><Representations><Representation>a</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sB"><Representations><Representation>b</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sD"><Representations><Representation>d</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sF"><Representations><Representation>f</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sG"><Representations><Representation>g</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sI"><Representations><Representation>i</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sK"><Representations><Representation>k</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sL"><Representations><Representation>l</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sN"><Representations><Representation>n</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sP"><Representations><Representation>p</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sT"><Representations><Representation>t</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sV"><Representations><Representation>v</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
      </SegmentDefinitions>
    </CharacterDefinitionTable>
    <NaturalClasses>
      <FeatureNaturalClass id="ncAny"><Name>Any</Name></FeatureNaturalClass>
      <!-- Branch C's mrZTagSlot requires this to prove the mandatory slot's rule is applicable
           (POS matches) but never actually fires on Branch C's own root or its partial rule's
           output: neither "nib" nor "nibgi" ends in "k", the class's only member. -->
      <SegmentNaturalClass id="ncOnlyK"><Name>OnlyK</Name><Segment segment="sK" /></SegmentNaturalClass>
    </NaturalClasses>
    <Strata>
      <Stratum characterDefinitionTable="tbl" morphologicalRuleOrder="unordered"
               morphologicalRules="mrGate1 mrGate2Partial mrGate2Complete mrGate3Partial"
               isActive="yes">
        <Name>Main</Name>
        <MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
          <!-- Branch A tag rules: template-only (never stratum-listed), so IsTemplateRule=true and
               exempt from both gates. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrFinTagA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posX" outputPartOfSpeech="posX">
            <Name>finTagA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subFinTagA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemFinTagA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemFinTagA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>fa</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>FINTAGA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>fintaga</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrNonFinTagA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posX" outputPartOfSpeech="posX">
            <Name>nonFinTagA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subNonFinTagA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemNonFinTagA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemNonFinTagA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>na</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NONFINTAGA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>nonfintaga</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- The Branch A ordinary rule under test: NOT partial, never a Slot member (stratum-listed
               only, below), so IsTemplateRule=false. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGate1" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posX" outputPartOfSpeech="posX">
            <Name>gate1</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGate1">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGate1"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemGate1" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ga</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GATE1</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>gate1</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- Branch B tag rules: template-only, exempt from both gates, same reasoning as Branch A. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrFinTagB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" outputPartOfSpeech="posY">
            <Name>finTagB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subFinTagB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemFinTagB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemFinTagB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>fb</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>FINTAGB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>fintagb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrNonFinTagB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" outputPartOfSpeech="posY">
            <Name>nonFinTagB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subNonFinTagB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemNonFinTagB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemNonFinTagB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>nb</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NONFINTAGB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>nonfintagb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- The Branch B ordinary rules under test, both stratum-listed only (never a Slot member,
               so both are IsTemplateRule=false): mrGate2Partial IS partial, mrGate2Complete is not. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGate2Partial" partial="true" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" outputPartOfSpeech="posY">
            <Name>gate2Partial</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGate2Partial">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGate2Partial"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemGate2Partial" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>vb</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GATE2PARTIAL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>gate2partial</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGate2Complete" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" outputPartOfSpeech="posY">
            <Name>gate2Complete</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGate2Complete">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGate2Complete"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemGate2Complete" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>tb</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GATE2COMPLETE</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>gate2complete</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- Branch C, isolated by posZ: pins the SynthesisAffixTemplatesRule.cs line-59
               pass-through (`!input.IsPartial && applicableTemplate`). mrGate3Partial (ordinary,
               partial="true", stratum-listed only) is tried on the root, making the WORD partial;
               templateZ (below) is applicable to posZ but its one mandatory slot's rule can never
               match the result, so the template battery yields zero output. Because the word is
               partial, line 59's `!input.IsPartial` is false and the ELSE branch runs: the word
               passes through unchanged with IsLastAppliedRuleFinal=true, closing the derivation
               with no template morpheme contributed. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrGate3Partial" partial="true" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posZ" outputPartOfSpeech="posZ">
            <Name>gate3Partial</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subGate3Partial">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemGate3Partial"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemGate3Partial" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>gi</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>GATE3PARTIAL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>gate3partial</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- templateZ's only slot, template-only (never stratum-listed, so IsTemplateRule=true,
               exempt from both gates: irrelevant here since it never actually applies, but kept
               consistent with the tag-rule convention above). Its MorphologicalInput requires the
               LAST segment to be in ncOnlyK ("k"), which mrGate3Partial's own tag ("gi") never
               satisfies, and neither does the bare root ("nib"), so this rule can never match
               either input state templateZ is tried against. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrZTagSlot" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posZ" outputPartOfSpeech="posZ">
            <Name>zTagSlot</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subZTagSlot">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemZTagSlot"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="0" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncOnlyK" /></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemZTagSlot" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>kv</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>ZTAGSLOT</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>ztagslot</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
        </MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
        <AffixTemplates>
          <!-- Branch A: final="true" is explicit (matches the default) so the red-on-revert mutation
               documented in words.yaml has a literal, present attribute to toggle. -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posX" final="true">
            <Name>finalTemplateA</Name>
            <Slot morphologicalRules="mrFinTagA"><Name>finTagSlotA</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posX" final="false">
            <Name>nonFinalTemplateA</Name>
            <Slot morphologicalRules="mrNonFinTagA"><Name>nonFinTagSlotA</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
          <!-- Branch B, isolated from Branch A by requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY". -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" final="true">
            <Name>finalTemplateB</Name>
            <Slot morphologicalRules="mrFinTagB"><Name>finTagSlotB</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posY" final="false">
            <Name>nonFinalTemplateB</Name>
            <Slot morphologicalRules="mrNonFinTagB"><Name>nonFinTagSlotB</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
          <!-- Branch C, isolated from A/B by requiredPartsOfSpeech="posZ". A single MANDATORY slot
               (no optional="true") so its rule's failure to match makes the whole template battery
               yield zero output for this template. -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posZ" final="true">
            <Name>templateZ</Name>
            <Slot morphologicalRules="mrZTagSlot"><Name>zTagSlot</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
        </AffixTemplates>
        <LexicalEntries>
          <LexicalEntry id="eDak" partOfSpeech="posX">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aDak"><PhoneticShape>dak</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>DAK</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>dak</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="ePil" partOfSpeech="posY">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aPil"><PhoneticShape>pil</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>PIL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>pil</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eNib" partOfSpeech="posZ">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aNib"><PhoneticShape>nib</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>NIB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>nib</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
        </LexicalEntries>
      </Stratum>
    </Strata>
  </Language>
</HermitCrabInput>
